<article class="env-corollary" id="E9B9DC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/E9B9DC">Corollary <span data-tag="E9B9DC">5.4.7.17</span>.</a>accessible!$\infty $-category of sections Let $p: X \rightarrow S$ be a map of simplicial sets which is a coCartesian fibration (or a Cartesian fibration). Assume that: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The simplicial set $S$ is small. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
For each vertex $s$ of $S$, the $\infty $-category $X_{s} = X \times _{S} \{ s\} $ is accessible. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(3)$"><p>
For each edge $e: s \rightarrow s'$ of $S$, the associated functor $X_{s} \rightarrow X_{s'}$ (or $X_{s'} \rightarrow X_{s}$) is accessible. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
  <p>Then $\bHom _{S}(S,X)$ is an accessible $\infty $-category. Moreover, if $\calC $ is accessible, then a functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[ \calC \rightarrow \bHom _{S}(S,X) \]
</div>
  <p> is accessible if and only if, for every vertex $s$ of $S$, the induced map $\calC \rightarrow X_{s}$ is accessible. </p>
</article> 
